      "summaries": {
        "en": "Promptfoo is an open-source framework for systematically testing and evaluating LLM prompts, agents, and RAG systems. It works by allowing developers to define test cases and expected behaviors in simple configuration files, then automatically runs these tests across multiple models like GPT and Claude to compare outputs. You can use it to catch prompt vulnerabilities, benchmark model performance, and integrate testing into CI/CD pipelines for reliable AI applications.",
        "zh": "Promptfoo 是一个开源框架，专门用于系统化测试和评估大语言模型的提示词、智能体及检索增强生成系统。它通过简单的配置文件定义测试用例和预期行为，自动在GPT、Claude等多种模型上运行对比，帮助开发者发现提示注入等安全隐患。其核心价值在于将软件工程的测试理念引入AI开发，你可以用它来验证提示词的稳定性，比较不同模型的输出质量，或将自动化测试集成到持续交付流程中，确保AI应用的可靠性。",
        "es": "Promptfoo is an open-source framework for systematically testing and evaluating LLM prompts, agents, and RAG systems. It works by allowing developers to define test cases and expected behaviors in simple configuration files, then automatically runs these tests across multiple models like GPT and Claude to compare outputs. You can use it to catch prompt vulnerabilities, benchmark model performance, and integrate testing into CI/CD pipelines for reliable AI applications.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "promptfoo stands out for ci, ci-cd, and cicd in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Promptfoo is an open-source framework for systematically testing and evaluating LLM prompts, agents, and RAG systems. It works by allowing developers to define test cases and expected behaviors in simple configuration files, then automatically runs these tests across multiple models like GPT and Claude to compare outputs. You can use it to catch prompt vulnerabilities, benchmark model performance, and integrate testing into CI/CD pipelines for reliable AI applications.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/promptfoo/promptfoo for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
