      "summaries": {
        "en": "IPED is an open-source digital forensics tool designed to process and analyze digital evidence from crime scenes or corporate investigations, addressing the need for accessible forensic analysis. It works by employing Java-based modular processing to extract, index, and search data from various digital sources, with a key insight being its ability to handle fragmented or deleted files through advanced recovery techniques. Users can apply it by loading evidence images, running automated analysis, and exploring results via its graphical interface, making it suitable for experimenting with forensic workflows or extending with custom plugins for specific data types.",
        "zh": "IPED是一款开源数字取证工具，用于处理和分析犯罪现场或企业调查中的数字证据，解决取证分析的可及性问题。它通过基于Java的模块化处理，从多种数字源提取、索引和搜索数据，其技术亮点在于利用高级恢复技术处理碎片化或已删除文件。用户可通过加载证据镜像、运行自动化分析并在图形界面中探索结果来应用它，适合实验取证流程或开发自定义插件以处理特定数据类型，为学习数字取证提供实践平台。",
        "es": "IPED is an open-source digital forensics tool designed to process and analyze digital evidence from crime scenes or corporate investigations, addressing the need for accessible forensic analysis. It works by employing Java-based modular processing to extract, index, and search data from various digital sources, with a key insight being its ability to handle fragmented or deleted files through advanced recovery techniques. Users can apply it by loading evidence images, running automated analysis, and exploring results via its graphical interface, making it suitable for experimenting with forensic workflows or extending with custom plugins for specific data types.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "IPED stands out for digital-forensics, forensic, and recovery in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "IPED is an open-source digital forensics tool designed to process and analyze digital evidence from crime scenes or corporate investigations, addressing the need for accessible forensic analysis. It works by employing Java-based modular processing to extract, index, and search data from various digital sources, with a key insight being its ability to handle fragmented or deleted files through advanced recovery techniques. Users can apply it by loading evidence images, running automated analysis, and exploring results via its graphical interface, making it suitable for experimenting with forensic workflows or extending with custom plugins for specific data types.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/sepinf-inc/IPED for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
